CORE
main.cpp
--unwind 5 --pointer-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* element copied from a parameter: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* evaluated per call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* mixed elements: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
__CPROVER_initialize
--
An element of a class type copy-initialized from an object (`{*p}' with a
pointer parameter p) is constructed by the copy constructor where the list
is evaluated ([dcl.init.list]/5).  It was the static initializer of the
backing array, which read the parameter in __CPROVER_initialize.
